; NOT built by default: mcp-kit is not on opam yet (it lives in a private repo — pin it from
; https://github.com/epure-team/ocaml-mcp, see docs/mcp-server.md). Set ARCH_MCP=yes to build it.
;
; `enabled_if` and NOT `(optional)`. (optional) only drops the *install* entry; the target stays
; in the directory's @all alias, which @default depends on, so `dune build` still fails with
; "Library mcp-kit.stdio not found". That is exactly how this broke CI. enabled_if removes the
; target from the rule set, so a checkout without the pin builds clean.
;
; %{env:...} in enabled_if is why dune-project is at (lang dune 3.15). %{lib-available:...} would
; auto-detect instead of needing the flag, but dune rejects it in an executable's enabled_if at
; every language version — checked up to 3.20.
;
; The `mcp` CI job sets ARCH_MCP=yes and asserts the .exe exists afterwards, so neither a stale
; target nor a silently-disabled one can pass unnoticed.
(executable
 (name arch_mcp)
 (public_name arch_mcp)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{env:ARCH_MCP=no} yes))
 (libraries arch_tools mcp-kit mcp-kit.stdio sqlite3 unix))
